<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The demon xenotypes' libido and heat genes lined up with the mods that ship equivalents.

		Gating, which is why this is its own folder: the demon xenotypes are not Heaven and Hell or Vampires and the
		Undead defs. Big and Small - Genes &amp; More defines them, inside a folder its own LoadFolders only loads when
		RedMattis.Undead or RedMattis.Heaven is active. This folder mirrors that exact condition.

		Changed from the original, on review: the succubus already carries VU_Libido_Succubus, and the original ADDED a
		second libido gene on top of it rather than replacing it, so a succubus ended up with two. Both operations are
		now replacements of VU_Libido_Succubus, which is what the same author's lilim patch in the Heaven and Hell file
		does. The two branches were already mutually exclusive, but Charmweavers used to win when both mods were
		installed; the check is now the other way round so the Highmate gene wins, as requested.
	-->
	<!--
		The succubus, hellguard, gatekeeper and imp gain Alpha Genes' heat immunity.

		Worth deciding before release: this is written as a plain addition, but the equivalent operation for the angels
		and Satan in the Heaven and Hell file removes MaxTemp_HugeIncrease and FireImmunity as it adds the Alpha Genes
		gene. All four of these demons carry both of those, so as written they end up with the Alpha Genes immunity on
		top of the two they already had. Adding the matching removals would make this a real swap, but that is a
		behaviour change, so the original is left alone here.
		Operations that also need another mod sit in a subfolder gated on it in loadFolders.xml.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_Succubus"]/genes/li[text()="VU_Libido_Succubus"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<li>VRE_Libido_VeryHigh</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
